cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SelCal, please cite it as below."
title: "SelCal: selection-aware calibration of scanned-lag dependence tests"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: BSD-3-Clause
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/lbiceice/selcal-software"
authors:
  - family-names: Liang
    given-names: Bingbing
    email: vincentdsnail@gmail.com
    affiliation: "School of AI Engineering, Guangzhou College of Technology and Business, Guangzhou, China; Faculty of Fine and Applied Arts, Khon Kaen University, Khon Kaen, Thailand"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-5344-0594"
keywords:
  - permutation test
  - circular-shift surrogate
  - lag selection
  - post-selection inference
  - time series
  - cross-correlation
abstract: >-
  SelCal tests lagged dependence between two time series when the lag is chosen
  by scanning a pre-declared set of candidate lags. It repeats the complete lag
  search inside every circular-shift surrogate, can enumerate the whole circular
  group exactly, refuses plans whose smallest attainable p-value exceeds alpha,
  and keeps verifiable, replayable records of every analysis.
